# Single-use migration scaffolding: never committed.
#
# land.sh reconstructs the four migration commits from the patches below; once
# those commits exist, git history carries the same changes with real authorship
# and these files are redundant. They stay on disk as an undo path until you are
# satisfied the viewer still behaves, then delete the directory contents.
#
# Committed neighbours in this directory: extract.mjs (reusable at the next
# upstream merge) and RECONSTRUCTION.md (how the source was recovered).
land.sh
*.patch
.land-dry.sh
